\", \"0\", \"2\", \"-\", \"0\", \"2\", \".\", \"j\", \"s\", \"o\", \"n\", \"h\", \"t\", \"t\", \"p\", \"s\", \":\", \"/\", \"/\", \"w\", \"w\", \"w\", \".\", \"c\", \"v\", \"e\", \".\", \"o\", \"r\", \"g\", \"/\", \"C\", \"V\", \"E\", \"R\", \"e\", \"c\", \"o\", \"r\", \"d\", \"?\", \"i\", \"d\", \"=\", \"C\", \"V\", \"E\", \"-\", \"2\", \"0\", \"2\", \"6\", \"-\", \"6\", \"5\", \"0\", \"5\", \"8\"]}\n        ```\n    *   **搜索引擎结果：**\n        ```\n        \n            ## 以下内容是基于此漏洞的搜索结果:\n                [webpage 0 begin] [title] Cve\n [description] Common vulnerabilities and Exposures (CVE) · We're sorry but the CVE Website doesn't work properly without JavaScript enabled. Please enable it to continue\n [link] https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2026-65058\n [webpage 0 end]\n[webpage 1 begin] [title] GitHub - SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs: A community-curated, verified collection of Proof-of-Concept exploits for CVEs disclosed in 2026. · GitHub\n [description] A community-curated, verified collection of Proof-of-Concept exploits for CVEs disclosed in 2026. - SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs\n [link] https://github.com/SecureWithUmer/CVE-2026-PoCs\n [webpage 1 end]\n[webpage 2 begin] [title] Exploit for CVE-2026-65058 - Industry News / Exploit Feed - KSEC Community Forum\n [description] 1 day ago - Proof-of-concept exploit for CVE-2026-65058. CVSS 5.9. This is a companion discussion topic for the original entry at https://sploitus.com/exploit?id=D9E9835C-8DFC-5780-8EE6-79A842138E12&utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss\n [link] https://forum.ksec.co.uk/t/exploit-for-cve-2026-65058/16791\n [webpage 2 end]\n[webpage 3 begin] [title] GitHub - XZ1r0/cve-2026-poc-collection: CVE-2026 PoC Collection - 128 PoCs covering 84 CVEs · GitHub\n [description] CVE-2026 PoC Collection - 128 PoCs covering 84 CVEs - XZ1r0/cve-2026-poc-collection\n [link] https://github.com/XZ1r0/cve-2026-poc-collection\n [webpage 3 end]\n[webpage 4 begin] [title] DayDayPoc\n [description] 登录 · poc提交 · 漏洞列表 · 漏洞环境 · 排行榜 · 插件下载 · 资产测绘 · 首页\n [link] https://www.ddpoc.com/\n [webpage 4 end]\n\n            \n        ```\n    *   **漏洞利用代码：**\n        ```\n        /tmp/dd7497a73bdeef8e2ef5210302af2fa2/README.md\n---\n# Trezor Safe Calldata Confirmation-Binding Bypass — CVE-2026-65058\n\n**Proof of Concept & Security Research**\n\n[![CVE](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVE-2026--65058-red)](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-65058)\n[![CVSS](https://img.shields.io/badge/CVSS-7.4-orange)](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-65058)\n[![Python](https://img.shields.io/badge/python-3.8%2B-blue)](https://python.org)\n[![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-green)](LICENSE)\n\nA critical vulnerability in Trezor Safe 3/5/7 firmware (< 2.8.7) that allows\nhidden calldata injection during transaction confirmation. The Trezor display\nshows only the first 256-byte chunk of calldata, but signs the ENTIRE payload —\ncreating a dangerous display/signing mismatch.\n\n## ⚠️ The Vulnerability\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────────┐\n│  TREZOR DISPLAY     │     │  WHAT TREZOR SIGNS      │\n│                     │     │                         │\n│  Transfer           │     │  Chunk 1: Transfer      │\n│  To: 0x742d...      │     │  Chunk 2: approve(∞) ← HIDDEN!\n│  Amount: 0.01 ETH   │     │                         │\n│                     │     │  SHA256(ALL chunks)     │\n│  User sees THIS ✓   │     │  User confirms THIS ✗   │\n└─────────────────────┘     └─────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n**Result**: User approves a small transfer, but the attacker gets unlimited\ntoken approval — enabling complete wallet drain.\n\n## Quick Start\n\n```bash\n# Clone\ngit clone https://github.com/iktok90-design/trezor-cve-2026-65058.git\ncd trezor-cve-2026-65058\n\n# Create virtual environment (recommended)\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\n\n# Install\npip install -r requirements.txt\n\n# Run demo\npython poc/bypass_poc.py --demo\n\n# Run self-test\npython poc/bypass_poc.py --self-test\n\n# Run all tests\npython -m pytest tests/ -v\n```\n\n## Project Structure\n\n```\ntrezor-cve-2026-65058/\n├── README.md                   # This file\n├── RESEARCH.md                 # Full research paper\n├── requirements.txt            # Python dependencies\n├── setup.py                    # Package installation\n├── poc/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── bypass_poc.py           # Main PoC — calldata bypass demo\n│   ├── calldata_injector.py    # Interactive calldata injection tool\n│   └── verify_fix.py           # Firmware fix verification\n├── tests/\n│   ├── __init__.py\n│   ├── test_calldata.py        # Unit tests for calldata logic\n│   └── test_vectors.py         # Known test vectors\n└── docs/\n    ├── CVE-2026-65058.md       # Detailed CVE documentation\n    ├── IMPACT.md               # Financial & security impact\n    └── MITIGATION.md           # How to protect yourself\n```\n\n## Key Findings\n\n| Finding | Detail |\n|---------|--------|\n| **Root Cause** | Calldata displayed ≠ calldata signed |\n| **Chunk Size** | 256 bytes per display chunk |\n| **Hidden Chunks** | All chunks after chunk 1 are invisible to user |\n| **Attack Vector** | Craft calldata: chunk 1 = benign, chunks 2+ = malicious |\n| **Result** | User confirms innocent operation, signs malicious one |\n| **Impact** | Full ERC-20 token drain (USDC, USDT, DAI, WBTC, etc.) |\n| **Fix** | Firmware 2.8.7 — displays ALL chunks, requires all confirmations |\n\n## Attack Demo\n\n```bash\n$ python poc/calldata_injector.py --visible transfer --hidden approve-usdt\n\n📱 TREZOR DISPLAYS TO USER:\n   Transfer: 0x742d35Cc... amount=0.010000 ETH\n\n🎭 HIDDEN OPERATIONS (not shown to user):\n   Chunk 2: approve(0xdAC17F95..., UNLIMITED)\n\n⚠️  MISMATCH: True\n   SHA256(displayed) ≠ SHA256(signed)\n```\n\n## Affected Devices\n\n- **Trezor Safe 3** — Firmware < 2.8.7\n- **Trezor Safe 5** — Firmware < 2.8.7\n- **Trezor Safe 7** — Firmware < 2.8.7\n\nTrezor Model T and Model One are **not affected**.\n\n## Fix & Mitigation\n\n1. **IMMEDIATELY**: Update to firmware >= 2.8.7 (the ONLY complete fix)\n2. **Review**: Check existing token approvals at [revoke.cash](https://revoke.cash)\n3. **Verify**: Run `python poc/verify_fix.py --self-test` to confirm fix behavior\n\nSee [`docs/MITIGATION.md`](docs/MITIGATION.md) for full guidance.\n\n## Timeline\n\n- **2026-07-15** — Vulnerability discovered\n- **2026-07-18** — Responsible disclosure to SatoshiLabs\n- **2026-07-22** — SatoshiLabs confirms and begins fix\n- **2026-07-25** — CVE-2026-65058 assigned\n- **2026-07-31** — Firmware 2.8.7 released\n- **2026-08-05** — Public disclosure & PoC release\n\n## Ethical Statement\n\nThis repository is published for:\n- **Security research** — understanding hardware wallet vulnerabilities\n- **Education** — teaching secure transaction confirmation design\n- **Verification** — enabling users to verify their devices are patched\n\nThis code should ONLY be used on devices you own, in controlled environments,\nand in accordance with applicable laws and Trezor's responsible disclosure\nguidelines.\n\n## License\n\nMIT License — See LICENSE file for details.\n\n## Contact\n\n- GitHub Issues: [Report a bug](https://github.com/iktok90-design/trezor-cve-2026-65058/issues)\n        ```\n\n    **你的角色：** 你是一名专业的网络安全分析师，擅长分析CVE漏洞信息。\n\n    **任务：**\n\n    1.  **CVE有效性：** 分析此CVE是否为真实存在的有效漏洞。请综合考虑CVE编号格式、漏洞描述的完整性、参考链接的存在、漏洞的技术细节等因素。\n    2.  **POC有效性：** 判断提供的POC代码是否有效，是否能实际利用此漏洞，并分析其有效性。\n    3.  **投毒风险：** 分析POC代码内容,判断此仓库中是否存在作者隐藏的投毒代码,分析结果使用百分比。务必不要把POC验证的后门代码判定为投毒代码。\n    4.  **利用方式：** 详细分析并总结漏洞的利用方式，包括攻击步骤、所需条件等。\n    5.  **代码分析：** 详细分析POC代码的工作原理、关键组件和执行流程。\n    6.  **排序优先级:** 搜索引擎结果 >  漏洞利用代码 > 漏洞库信息\n    7.  **输出内容:** 务必使用中文\n    8.  **markdown内容:** 务必使用markdown格式，包含以下部分：\n        - 漏洞概述\n        - 有效性分析\n        - 投毒风险分析\n        - 利用方式\n        - 代码分析\n    **输出格式：**  你**必须**严格按照以下 **JSON** 格式输出，**不要包含任何额外的文字、说明或前缀/后缀**。JSON中的**所有键和字符串类型的值必须使用双引号**。请务必对特殊字符进行转